{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4968-revised-arete","id":4968,"title":"Revised Arete?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T05:04:40-08:00","id":4968,"title":"Revised Arete?","content":"So: while I simply love the concept of Arete, its implementation leaves something to be desired IMHO. \u201cMore dice\u201d is boring \u2014 often necessary, but boring nonetheless. What I\u2019d like to see out of Arete would be to treat it as an \u201cEpic Skills\u201d system, exactly analogous to Epic Attributes up to and including the ability to acquire Feats (which would be to Epic Skills as Knacks are to Epic Attributes). <br /> <br /> The trick lies in coming up with a way to handle Feats that doesn\u2019t explode the page count required for Arete. The way I\u2019ve been doing it so far has been to borrow heavily from the \u201cSkill Tricks\u201d rules found in <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b>: establish a few standard mechanics that can be used to build new Feats, give a few example Feats that are fully worked out (representing some of the more well-known feats performed in greek mythology), and giving starting points for two or three more per skill. I would expect a later supplement dedicated to the greek gods to expand on the list of fully worked out Feats considerably. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:37:04-08:00","id":8151,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with the Feats in World of Darkness: Mirrors, but it sounds similar to what I wanted to Arete to become. In my mind Arete should work somewhat similar to Solar charms in Exalted. Flashy, epic actions that one sees in classical mythology. Its not just simply being better at the skill but that there is almost a boasting quality to what is being demonstrated by sheer dint of its, well..awesomeness. Knacks for skills sounds like a great idea, though the authors would need to be careful with overlap with regular Knacks and make the abilities really tailored for the skill in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:25:39-08:00","id":8199,"title":"","content":"Yeah; <b>Exalted</b> is indeed a goldmine of inspiration for devising Feats for use with Arete. My main qualm with it is the \u201cmote economy\u201d and the massive Charm Trees. <b>Scion</b> would need something with far less crunch involved. That\u2019s why I used <b>Mirrors</b>\u2019 Skill Tricks as my point of reference: like <b>Exalted</b>\u2019s Charms, Skill Tricks represent particular uses of a skill in which the character excels; but instead of a massive network of them, you\u2019re given three examples per skill and the tools to make more. And also unlike Charms, there\u2019s no \u201cfuel economy\u201d to mess with. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s also worth noting that <b>Trinity Continuum</b>\u2019s Talents are essentially the same concept; and while <b>Scion</b> and <b>Trinity Continuum</b> are separate gamelines, they <i>are</i> going to share a common game system. It would be nice if greek scions and TC\u2019s Talents could implement their \u201cremarkable competence\u201d mechanics in ways that at least complement each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:00:43-08:00","id":8230,"title":"","content":"I feel like the idea of &quot;epic abilities&quot; should not be restricted to Dodekathon Scions exclusively. That's not to say that something of this sort is not tonally appropriate for Arete, just that abilities need a bit more of a reason to focus on them, and this seems like a way to create that focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T21:28:23-08:00","id":14518,"title":"","content":"I'm not asking you to copy the entire section of the book, but an you give us an example of what some skill tricks are for those who do not have the book nor play nWoD all that much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T22:07:30-08:00","id":14534,"title":"","content":"Skill Tricks are first divided into five categories: Combat (obvious, only special rule is that these are always rolled), Extra Talent (dice adder), Penalty (dice penalty to target the character), Story Advancement (basically a narrative pass on a plot point), Time Saver (again obvious).<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Dismantle (Firearms, Combat) - render an opponent's gun inoperable by removing a key component.<br /> <br /> Trick Shot (Firearms, Extra Talent or Story Advancement) - can do trick shots and either get bonus dice when actively messing with another character (shooting a gun out of their hand) or to automatically disable something in the way of the plot (a door lock).<br /> <br /> Homemade Tools (Survival, Time Saver) - can make tools out of natural materials, so you can always have a useful tool handy rather than having to go looking for one or taking lots of time to craft them.<br /> <br /> Will-o'-the-Wisp (Survival, Penalty) - subtract dice from opponents in combat by using the environment against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}